  "headline": "Westpac's credit impairment charge fell $113 million to $424 million in FY25 from $537 million in FY24, a 21% reduction. The loss rate on average loans declined from 7 bps to 5 bps. The improvement was driven mainly by a $174 million swing in individually assessed provisions (IAPs) — from a $140 million net charge to a $34 million net benefit — due to higher write-backs (+$102m) and recoveries (+$57m), partly offset by a $61 million increase in collectively assessed provision (CAP) charges, primarily from higher write-offs (+$75m). Divisionally, Institutional swung from a $120 million charge to a $1 million benefit (+$121m) and New Zealand from a $25 million charge to a $41 million benefit (+$66m), while Business & Wealth saw its charge rise $103 million to $245 million.",
